<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lower Valais</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valais">Valais</a> is the French-speaking western part of the canton of Valais in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhone">Rhône</a> from below Sion to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-geneva">Lake Geneva</a>. Conquered in stages from Savoy by the German-speaking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-valais">Upper Valais</a> in 1475 and 1536, it was ruled as a subject territory until 1798, when it rose with French support. It then became an equal part of the Valais, which joined the Swiss Confederation as a canton in 1815.</p></div>
